hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20941","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Dhayyal ibn Ubayd ibn Hanzalah narrated to us, he said: I heard Hanzalah ibn Hidhaym, my grandfather, that his grandfather Hanifah said to Hidhaym: Gather my sons for me, for I want to bequeath. So he gathered them, and he said: The first of what I bequeath is that to this orphan of mine in my care belong one hundred camels which we called in the Jahiliyyah al-Mutayyabah. Hidhaym said: O father, I heard your sons say: We only acknowledge this before our father, and when he dies we take it back. He said: Between me and you is the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Hidhaym said: We agree. So Hidhaym and Hanifah and Hanzalah went up, with them a boy riding behind Hidhaym. When they came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, they greeted him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What brought you, O Abu Hidhaym. He said: This, and he struck with his hand upon the thigh of Hidhaym. He said: I feared old age or death would come suddenly upon me, so I wanted to bequeath, and I said: The first of what I bequeath is that to this orphan of mine in my care belong one hundred camels we called in the Jahiliyyah al-Mutayyabah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, became angry until we saw anger in his face, he was sitting and knelt upon his knees and said: No, no, no. Charity is five, otherwise ten, otherwise fifteen, otherwise twenty, otherwise twenty-five, otherwise thirty, otherwise thirty-five, and if many then forty. He said: They bade him farewell, and with the orphan was a stick beating a camel, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Great is this staff of an orphan. Hanzalah said: He brought me near to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I have sons with beards and younger than that, and this is the youngest of them, so pray to Allah for him. So he wiped his head and said: May Allah bless you, or blessed be in him. Dhayyal said: I saw Hanzalah brought a man with swollen face or a beast with swollen udder, and he spits upon his hands and says: In the name of Allah, and places his hand upon his head and says: Upon the place of the hand of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then wipes it upon him. Dhayyal said: The swelling goes away."
